    "summary": "A few of the comments that stood out to us yesterday: \"Many of you have expressed respect and admiration for Henri Chemin as a team director and as a pilot. I know Henri personally for near 15 years now and can tell you he is an outstanding man. For the benefit of the BAT community I want to make you aware of the multitude of things he has done in his career and the many accomplished figures he has had close relationships with and impacts on. Now 93 years old, living between Nice and Antibes, and still very much a competitive soul, suffice it&#8230;\" 9 RomTNT commented on No Reserve: Ex–Ecurie Chrysler France 1970 Plymouth Hemi ’Cuda 4-Speed \"Maybe it's me being sentimental, but Burnt Orange Metallic is my favorite Mopar color, likely because my first car was a 1970 Dodge Charger R/T in FK5. Black vinyl top, black tail stripe and black interior set it apart from this Charger (and the fact that it was an R/T), but I can't help but get all warm-feeling inside from looking at this one. It's beautiful...\" 6 gtrdave commented on One-Family-Owned 1970 Dodge Charger 500 V8 \"I used to own a 1986 560 SEC. Although the 380 won't have the same power, everything else about this car is still excellent. Its quiet, its smooth, its durable, and I got compliments on the car everywhere. The pillarless coupe look gave the car an aggressively futuristic shape for the blocky 1980s, and I'm convinced this generation is one of the best in all of Mercedes history. Good luck to all, whoever gets this car will not be disappointed!\" 5 AnachronIstClassicCars commented on No Reserve: 1983 Mercedes-Benz 380SEC \"Still one of the best looking modern M cars. Hard to beat a naturally aspirated V8 in a coupe.\" 6 BadCreditGoodTaste commented on 2012 BMW M3 Coupe Competition Package Track Car",
